## Core Principles

### I. Code Quality
**MUST** write clean, maintainable, and well-documented code. Code reviews are mandatory before merging.

### II. Testing
**MUST** write tests for all critical functionality. Aim for high test coverage without gaming metrics.

### III. Security
**MUST** follow security best practices. Never commit secrets. Validate all inputs.

### IV. Documentation
**MUST** document all public APIs and complex logic. Keep documentation up-to-date with code changes.

### V. Performance
**SHOULD** consider performance implications. Optimize hot paths. Profile before optimizing.

## {{.AppKind}}-Specific Guidelines

{{if eq .AppKind "CLI"}}### CLI Best Practices
- Provide helpful error messages
- Support --help flag for all commands
- Follow POSIX conventions for flags
- Exit with appropriate exit codes
{{else if eq .AppKind "web"}}### Web Application Best Practices
- Implement proper error handling
- Use HTTPS in production
- Validate and sanitize all inputs
- Implement rate limiting
{{else}}### Service Best Practices
- Implement health checks
- Log structured data
- Handle graceful shutdown
- Monitor resource usage
{{end}}

